SUMMARY:🍁🎄Fall Niagara Falls Hiking Day Trip — Trails\, Dinner & F
 estival of Lights!!
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 15 Years!\n# 🍁
 🎄 Niagara Falls Fall Hiking Trip & Winter Festival of Lights! 🌈\n\n
 🌦️ **RAIN OR SHINE!**\n\nThe adventure goes on\, whether we're enjoyi
 ng golden sunshine\, crisp autumn air\, or a little mist from the Falls. A
 fter a day of hiking\, we'll finish with dinner and the spectacular Winter
  Festival of Lights! ✨\n\n***\n\n## 🥾 About the Trip\n\nLet's escape 
 the city for a full day of fresh air\, friendship\, and breathtaking scene
 ry! We'll explore the natural side of Niagara Falls — less time in the t
 ourist crowds\, more trails\, trees\, and spectacular views.\n\nWe'll meet
  outside the **Fairmont Royal York on Front Street West**\, travel togethe
 r by GO Train to Niagara Falls\, and make our way to **Niagara Glen Nature
  Reserve** for a hike among ancient boulders\, winding forest paths\, and 
 the turquoise waters of the Niagara River.\n\nThe trail features stairs\, 
 uneven ground\, elevation changes\, and a climb back up out of the gorge. 
 This is a proper hike\, so please read the expectations below before signi
 ng up.\n\n**A Special Guest Joining Us!**\n\nWe're excited to welcome Mile
 s Howard\, visiting us from Boston on November 14–15!\n\nMiles is writin
 g *HIKE EVERY CITY*\, a book (coming in 2028) exploring urban hiking\, com
 munity\, and how exploring cities on foot brings people together. He also 
 runs a similar urban hiking project in Boston called *Walking City Trails*
 .\n\nHe'll be joining us for both weekend outings\, including Niagara Fall
 s\, to experience our group firsthand and meet our members.\nFeel free to 
 say hello\, share your experiences\, and chat with Miles if you'd like. No
  pressure\, of course!\n\nIt's exciting to see our community getting notic
 ed beyond Toronto. Let's give Miles a warm welcome!\n\n***\n\n## 🌲 The 
 Trail Experience\n\nNiagara Glen is a beautiful natural area carved into t
 he Niagara Gorge over thousands of years. We'll follow forest trails\, tak
 e photos\, enjoy the fall colours\, and experience a side of Niagara Falls
  that many visitors never see.\n\nThe planned hike is approximately **4 km
 **\, although the terrain makes it more demanding than the distance might 
 suggest. We'll have opportunities to pause and enjoy the scenery\, but eve
 ryone needs to be prepared for the physical demands of the route.\n\n### 
 ⚠️🥾 IMPORTANT: HIKE EXPECTATIONS — PLEASE READ CAREFULLY 🥾⚠
 ️\n\n**This is a real hiking trail\, not a casual walk.**\nBefore signin
 g up\, please be confident that you can:\n\n* ✔️ Walk for an extended 
 period of time.\n* ✔️ Handle uneven terrain\, stairs\, elevation chang
 es\, and the climb back up out of the gorge.\n* ✔️ Keep up with the gr
 oup at a steady pace without needing frequent or extended stops.\n* ✔️
  Manage a full day of walking\, travel\, dinner\, and evening sightseeing.
 \n\n**This is not the event to use to test your fitness level or see how t
 hings go.** If you're unsure whether you can complete the hike\, please ch
 oose an easier event instead.\nIf you find yourself unable to keep up\, yo
 u may need to turn back or continue independently where the route and circ
 umstances allow.\n\nThe group cannot stop or slow down significantly to ac
 commodate someone who is struggling\, as this affects the experience and s
 chedule for everyone.\nPlease make an honest assessment of your abilities 
 before committing. The goal is to keep the day safe\, enjoyable\, and on t
 rack for the entire group.\n\n***\n\n## 🍔 Dinner at Chuck's Roadhouse\n
 \nAfter the hike\, we'll head to **Chuck's Roadhouse on Clifton Hill** for
  a relaxed dinner. Everyone is responsible for the cost of their own meal.
 \n\n⚠️ **Please note:** The restaurant has limited vegetarian options.
  If this means you won't be joining us for dinner\, please let me know in 
 advance so I can plan the numbers. Please don't leave this until the last 
 minute\, as I'll be arranging the dinner headcount.\n\n***\n\n## 🎇 Wint
 er Festival of Lights\n\nAfter dinner\, we'll head down to the Falls to en
 joy the **Niagara Falls Winter Festival of Lights**.\nThe surrounding area
  comes alive with illuminated displays and colourful seasonal installation
 s. We'll take a relaxed evening stroll\, enjoy the atmosphere\, and stop f
 or photos along the way.\nBring warm layers — temperatures near the Fall
 s can drop\, especially after dark! 🧣✨\n\n***\n\n## 💲 Meetup Fee\n
 \n**$5 Meetup fee**\n💵 Cash at the event\, or\n📧 E-transfer to **[ma
 thewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)** before or on 
 the day.\n\n***\n\n## 🚆 TRANSPORTATION REQUIREMENT — PLEASE READ\n\n*
 *Everyone must travel with the group on the GO Train to participate in thi
 s event.**\nWe will not meet people separately in Niagara Falls. Travellin
 g together helps us coordinate the day's activities\, stay on schedule\, a
 nd avoid confusion about meeting points and transportation.\nPlease arrive
  on time at our Toronto meeting point. We will not be able to hold the tra
 in for late arrivals.\n\n***\n\n## 🕒 Travel Details (Approximate)\n\n* 
 **8:15 AM** — Meet outside the main doors of the Fairmont Royal York on 
 Front Street West. Look for my Moose Hat! 🫎\n* **8:30 AM** — Depart f
 or the GO Train.\n* **9:03 AM** — Planned GO Train departure for Niagara
  Falls.\n* **11:25 AM** — Expected arrival in Niagara Falls.\n* **12:30 
 PM** — Planned start of the Niagara Glen hike.\n* **4:30 PM** — Dinner
  at Chuck's Roadhouse.\n* **6:00 PM** — Head down to the Falls for the W
 inter Festival of Lights.\n* **8:00–9:00 PM** — Target return-train wi
 ndow to Toronto.\n\n🚆 These times are approximate and depend on the tra
 nsit schedule and conditions on the day. I'll share any necessary updates 
 closer to the event. Please check the current GO Transit schedule before p
 urchasing your ticket.\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Tickets & What to Bring\n\nPle
 ase purchase the **GO + WEGO Combo Ticket** in advance. The previously lis
 ted round-trip price was approximately $20\, but please check the current 
 price and service details before buying.\n👉 **[Click here for the Niaga
 ra Parks GO + WEGO offer](https://www.gotransit.com/en/partners-and-promot
 ions/go-train-to-niagara-on-weekends)**\n\nBring:\n\n* 🥾 Sturdy walking
  shoes or hiking boots with good grip.\n* 💧 Water and snacks.\n* 🧥 W
 arm layers for the evening.\n* 📸 A camera or charged phone.\n* 🎒 Any
 thing else you need for a full day outdoors.\n\n***\n\n## ⚠️ Important
  Notes\n\n* This is a full\, active day involving a train journey\, a hike
 \, dinner\, and evening sightseeing.\n* The event is open to everyone — 
 singles\, couples\, and friends — provided they can manage the hike.\n* 
 Please RSVP only if you understand the physical requirements and can commi
 t to the day's itinerary.\n* You can RSVP ahead of time or show up on the 
 day if you're unsure about your schedule\, but please remember that the tr
 ain arrangements and group itinerary require punctuality.\n* Sometimes thi
 ngs happen and I may need to cancel or change the plans. Please watch the 
 event page for updates.\n\n***\n\n👤 **Organized by Mathew**\nQuestions?
  Post on the event wall or email **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](m
 ailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**.\n\n**Come for the hike.**\n*
 *Stay for the lights.**\n**Leave with a full day of adventure and new conn
 ections.** 🍁🎄
