SUMMARY:🍁Fall Hike: Long Branch GO to Port Credit GO🍁
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 15 Years!\n# 🍁 
 Fall Hike: Long Branch GO to Port Credit GO\n\nJoin us for a scenic lakesi
 de hike along the beautiful Waterfront Trail\, from Long Branch GO Station
  to Port Credit GO Station!\n\nWe’ll explore a mix of parks\, beaches\, 
 and tree-lined paths\, taking in the crisp autumn air\, colourful leaves\,
  and classic Lake Ontario views. This is the first time our group has done
  this particular route\, so come along and help us welcome the fall season
 !\n\nWe’ll take our time\, with stops for photos\, snacks\, and conversa
 tion along the way. This is a social hike rather than a race\, but please 
 be prepared to walk for a few hours. We’ll finish in Port Credit\, where
  we’ll take the GO train back toward Toronto.\n\n***\n\n### 🚆 Meetup 
 Details — Choose Your Starting Point\n\n**Option 1: Meet in Toronto and 
 travel together**\n📍 **Meeting location:** Outside the main doors of th
 e Fairmont Royal York on Front Street West.\n\n* **10:15 AM:** Meet outsid
 e the hotel. Look for my Moose Hat! 🦌\n* **10:30 AM sharp:** We’ll le
 ave for the station.\n* **10:45 AM:** Planned train departure.\n\nPlease a
 rrive on time. We cannot hold the train for latecomers\, and once we’ve 
 left\, you’ll need to make your own way to the starting point if you mis
 s us.\n\n**Option 2: Meet us at Long Branch GO Station**\n\n📍 **Meeting
  location:** Long Branch GO Station\, **by the station exit closest to the
  parking lot**.\n\nThis is our starting point for the hike. Please meet me
  by that exit and look for the Moose Hat! 🦌\n\n* **Around 11:00 AM:** A
 rrive and find the group.\n* **11:15 AM:** We’ll begin the walk.\n\nPlea
 se use the specified exit rather than waiting elsewhere around the station
 . We had some confusion with the meeting point previously\, so make sure y
 ou know where to find us.\n\n**Important:** This is a point-to-point hike.
  We’ll finish at **Port Credit GO Station**\, not Long Branch. We will n
 ot walk back to Long Branch.\n\n### 🥾 The Walk\n\nWe’ll follow the Wa
 terfront Trail through a mix of waterfront scenery\, parks\, beaches\, and
  paths. We’ll take occasional breaks for photos\, snacks\, and conversat
 ion\, with time to enjoy the views and each other’s company.\n\nPlease w
 ear comfortable walking shoes and be prepared for a few hours on your feet
 . Bring your own water and snacks\; you’re welcome to bring something ex
 tra to share.\n\n### 🚆 Getting Back\n\nWe expect to start wrapping up a
 round **2:00 PM**\, with our destination being Port Credit GO Station.\n\n
 We’ll take the GO train from Port Credit toward Toronto. **Please check 
 the GO schedule for the event date before attending.** Not every train nec
 essarily stops at Long Branch\, so do not assume you can take the train ba
 ck there to retrieve a car. If you’re driving and parking at Long Branch
 \, check your return options in advance.\n\n### 💲 Meetup Fee\n\nThe Mee
 tup fee is **$5**\, payable in cash in person or by e-transfer to **[mathe
 wmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**.\nGO train fares
  are additional. Check the current fare for your journey.\n\n### 🎒 What
  to Bring\n\n* Water\n* Comfortable walking shoes\n* Snacks or something s
 mall for our breaks\n* A camera or phone for the fall colours\n* Weather-a
 ppropriate clothing\n\n### ⚠️ Please Note\n\n* This event is weather-d
 ependent only if conditions make the walk unsafe. Keep an eye on the event
  page for any updates or cancellation notices.\n* You’re welcome to leav
 e early\, but please let me know so I know you’ve left the group.\n* If 
 you’re joining at Long Branch\, make sure you use the **station exit clo
 sest to the parking lot**.\n* This is a one-way walk ending at Port Credit
 . Please plan your transportation accordingly.\n\n### 👥 About the Group
 \n\nWhether you’re single or partnered\, you’re welcome to join us to 
 get outdoors\, meet people\, and make connections. We also organize movies
 \, walks\, hikes\, arts and culture outings\, restaurant visits\, and plen
 ty more.\nOrganized by Mathew. Questions? Post on the event wall or email 
 **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hot
 mail.com)**.\n\n🍁 Enjoy the trail. Take in the views. Meet some new peo
 ple.
