SUMMARY:🌰 Hogg’s Hollow Fall Walk & Lunch! 🍂!
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 15 Years!\n### 
 🌰 Hogg’s Hollow Fall Walk & Lunch! 🍂\n\nJoin us for a beautiful fa
 ll walk through Hogg’s Hollow\, one of Toronto’s charming historic nei
 ghbourhoods tucked away in North York. With its winding roads\, forested t
 rails\, stone bridges\, and scenic ravines\, this area feels like a hidden
  village in the middle of the city — especially when the leaves turn gol
 den and the air starts to feel like autumn.\n\nWe’ll explore the valley 
 around the Don River West Branch\, taking in the neighbourhood’s natural
  beauty and historic character. Along the way\, we’ll touch on the story
  of James Hogg\, the Scottish settler associated with the area’s early m
 ill\, and the tragic **Hogg’s Hollow Disaster of 1960**\, when five work
 ers lost their lives during tunnel construction.\n\nAfter our walk\, we’
 ll head to **Swiss Chalet** for lunch\, because nothing says fall like com
 fort food and good company! 🍗\n\n### 📍 Meetup Location — Please Re
 ad Carefully!\n\n**We’re meeting directly in front of the Shell gas stat
 ion store entrance.**\nPlease stand **right in front of the entrance to th
 e store**\, where people walk in and out.\nLook for my famous Moose Hat! 
 🦌\n\n### 🕒 Meetup Details\n\n* **Meeting time:** 11:00 AM\n* **Depar
 ture:** 11:05 AM sharp. I’ll wait a maximum of five minutes.\n* **Ending
  location:** We’ll return to our starting point\, making it convenient f
 or anyone arriving by transit or car.\n* **Meetup fee:** $5\, payable in c
 ash or by e-transfer to **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean
 @hotmail.com)**.\n\n### 🥾 What to Bring\n\n* Water\n* Comfortable walki
 ng shoes\n* A snack if you’d like something before lunch\n* Weather-appr
 opriate clothing\n\n☔ **Rain or shine!** There’s no such thing as bad 
 weather — just inappropriate clothing.\n\n### 👥 About the Group\n\nWh
 ether you’re single or partnered\, you’re welcome to join us to get ou
 tdoors\, meet people\, and make connections. We also organize movies\, wal
 ks\, hikes\, arts and culture outings\, restaurant visits\, and plenty mor
 e.\n**You can RSVP ahead of time or show up on the day** if you’re not s
 ure you can make it.\n\nOrganized by Mathew. Questions? Post on the event 
 wall or email **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomovies
 andoutings@hotmail.com)**.\n\n🍂 Enjoy the walk. Stay for lunch. Leave w
 ith new connections.
