SUMMARY:🏀 Huskies vs. Phoenix: Basketball\, Wings & Good Company!
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 15 Years!\n# 🏀 
 Huskies vs. Phoenix: Basketball\, Wings & Good Company!\n\nYou don't have 
 to be a sports fanatic to enjoy a good basketball game! Sometimes it's abo
 ut cheering on a friend\, getting out for the evening\, and having some fu
 n with a great group of people.\n\nWe're heading to George Brown College's
  St. James Campus to watch the **George Brown Huskies take on the Fleming 
 Phoenix** in a college basketball matchup.\n\nI have a personal connection
  to both the game and the school: George Brown is my alma mater\, where I 
 graduated as a Child and Youth Worker\, and a friend of mine coaches the F
 leming team. So I'm heading out to support my friend and enjoy an evening 
 of basketball.\n\nCome join me!\n\n🏀 **The Game Plan**\n\n* **6:30 PM:*
 * Meet outside the main doors of George Brown College's St. James Campus. 
 Look for my Moose Hat!\n* **6:35 PM:** We'll head inside and make our way 
 to the gymnasium. There may be other activities happening before tip-off\,
  so we'll get settled and see what's going on.\n* **7:00 PM:** Tip-off! Le
 t's cheer on the teams and enjoy the game.\n* **After the game:** We'll he
 ad over to St. Louis Bar & Grill on King Street for wings\, food\, and con
 versation. This part is completely optional\, so you're welcome to join us
  for the game and head home afterward.\n\nI'll wait five minutes at our me
 eting spot before heading inside\, so arrive on time if you want to come i
 n with the group.\n\n🍗 **Why Stop at Basketball?**\n\nThe best part of 
 getting together is often what happens afterward. Whether you're a basketb
 all fan\, a George Brown alum\, or someone who just enjoys meeting new peo
 ple\, this is a chance to share an experience\, have a few laughs\, and ma
 ke some new connections.\n\n**A few things to know:**\n\n* **No Meetup fee
 !** (Free event\, real commitment!)\n* Food and drinks afterward are optio
 nal\, and everyone pays for their own order.\n* You don't need to know any
 thing about basketball to join us. Enthusiasm\, curiosity\, or a willingne
 ss to enjoy the evening is more than enough.\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n
 \nThis group is for people who want to be social\, make friends\, and enjo
 y time together — whether single or partnered.\nWe organize movies\, wal
 ks\, hikes\, restaurant outings\, arts and culture events\, karaoke\, and 
 plenty more.\n\n👤 **Organized by Mathew.**\nQuestions? Post on the even
 t wall or email **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomovi
 esandoutings@hotmail.com)**.\n\nCome for the basketball\, stay for the win
 gs\, and leave with a few new connections! 🏀🍗
